    ],
    "notes": "canonical muxed account ids (uint64, 0 to 2^64-1). accepted cases carry the M address and MuxedAccount XDR for key 0x3a..3a with that id. text is canonical only as the exact decimal rendering of an in-range value, and refused with a sign (including -0), whitespace, a radix prefix, an exponent, non-ASCII digits, when empty or out of range; a JSON number is canonical as an integer in range with |n| <= 2^53-1, and refused when negative, non-integral or out of range. leading-zero text, integral numbers written with .0 and in-range numbers above 2^53-1 are in a separate implementation-defined entry. the reject reason is informational; a testee passes by refusing.",
